      "value": "@{6283e1007316fe0b7ef81f7f|full_name} \n\nEDIT:don't read this too seriously, I think I wasn't thinking alright when I wrote it.\n\nThanks for the reply. You have very good points. And I believe I understand it. Tell me if I don't. \n\nHere's my thought on your reply. I am being extreme on this.\n\n1.  Yeah, not directly. Anything can help anything indirectly. It's not a problem that exists now, so it's ok to ignore for now. But in a extreme cases (such as mandatory verification) I think it will. And VRChat probably need to take some action about it. And I have a question, how does it help us being trustworthy?\n\n2. Nothing to say about it, I do think it's okay to have age gated instances, which help things somewhat manageable.\n\n3. Yeah, agreed, they don't look shady company now. For this topic, I feel I need to learn more about it to know A. why ID is needed to sent them and how it isn't ID verification at all, B. how I verify if they deleted it, or trust they did other than their promise (again, I am being extreme on it). Are there good resources to help understanding it?\n\nThanks for the link as well. I did a quick look at it. I'll pick up keywords and search more later.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
